  "notes": "Game lighting crushed the navy to near-black so navy lifted to #2b40a8 (value +25%); red restaurant deeper less pink (#b81c25); corner transoms 3 rows of 0.26 m lights (divided-light muntins). Masonic face: two narrow windows with a 0.85 m bulkhead instead of a tall glazed curtain; colourful shop stock (plants, yellow, magenta, blue). Sign boards are clean blank faces (no glyph strokes that read as gibberish); more saturated navy (#2b40a8) so the corner shop stays navy under game light; black-section cornice is a dark projecting wood band (no flat dentil stripe). Saturated deep navy corner shop (#1d2552) with a boxed navy sign cabinet (abstract text-free glyph strokes, gooseneck lamps) and modelled scroll brackets with modillions under the cornice; packed, lit window displays (dark back board, stepped shelves of coloured goods) behind every storefront pane so the glass shows merchandise instead of a pale empty room; a big boxed sign over the right black shop and tan scroll brackets over the black section; festoon catenary string lights (sagging wire, hanging emissive bulbs); the red restaurant gets a boxed illuminated white-face sign and a dark lettered lower sign board in place of the plain band; taller transom band on the corner shop; pendant shop lights over the sales floor. Corner shop deep navy (not royal blue); black bays glazed behind the gates with a continuous warm-lit multipane transom band over each shop and a tan bracketed cornice above the black section; brighter silver gates in grey frames over one opening only; red restaurant gets a lit (text-free) lightbox sign band under the red fascia; interior split per shop (`shopFitout` partitions with mid-tone linings) with folded-garment stack tables and a muted stock palette. Royal-blue corner shop (brighter, kickplates with white pinstripes, taller transom band), silver diamond scissor gates in black cast-iron frames, string lights across the black shop, a navy sign band and round sign disc on a glossier red restaurant front, denser stock. Per-shop dressing through the new `shopBays` builder key - navy corner shop in three tiers (tall multipane display bays, a band of small multipane transom lights, a navy sign fascia under a bracketed, dentilled cornice), gated shop with dark scissor-lattice gates and two big multipane windows above, black shop with a low storefront, sign band and small lit windows above, red restaurant framed by red pilasters with a clerestory strip, an inset black sign band and a frieze under the parapet; corner pier and fascia wrap onto Masonic; shelves, rails and wall runs stocked (`shopStock`); reflective storefront glass. 1906 one-storey row of five shops, S side of Haight Street at the SW corner of Masonic (1401-1419). Tall commercial storey with a flat roof, short parapet and thin cornice; painted stucco in zones: a deep navy corner shop with full-height glazing and a multipane clerestory band that wraps onto Masonic, two black-painted shops (one behind two white folding lattice gates, one glazed with a centre door), and a red restaurant front with an open glazed face. Masonic face navy with large windows near the corner and a painted colour-field panel at the south end.",
